.TH PACK 1 "September 2026" "TdeZip Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pack, unpack, pcat \- compress and expand files using Huffman coding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pack
[\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-c\fR] [\fB\-v\fR] \fIfile\fR ...
.PP
.B unpack
[\fB\-f\fR] [\fB\-c\fR] [\fB\-v\fR] \fIfile\fR ...
.PP
.B pcat
[\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pack
compresses the specified files using a two-pass canonical Huffman coding algorithm,
originally designed by T.G. Szymanski for Research Unix.
The compressed files are given the suffix
.B .z
and retain the access modes, modification dates, and ownership of the original files.
If compression is successful and \fB\-c\fR is not specified, the original uncompressed
file is removed.
.PP
.B unpack
restores files previously packed by
.BR pack .
The
.B .z
suffix may be omitted from input filenames.
Upon successful decompression, the
.B .z
archive is removed (unless \fB\-c\fR is specified).
.PP
.B pcat
decompresses files to standard output without removing the original packed file.
If no files are specified,
.B pcat
reads packed data from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Force packing even if no file size reduction occurs. When unpacking, overwrite
existing files without error.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-stdout
Write compressed or decompressed output to standard output, leaving original files untouched.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Display compression statistics or decompression progress.
.SH AUTHORS
Originally written by Thomas G. Szymanski (Bell Laboratories, 1978\(en1979).
Modernized and packaged for Trinity Desktop Environment (TDE) / TdeZip.
